    "Exact85c06ee/SDK7cb474, native intro, X/P1 and normal Zero/P2, shared native4:3 OpenGL/stacked meters, ordinary published input, dummy muted audio; same-machine Win64 loopback only.",
    "Each character dies separately from original enemy contact after observed actual native motion. Consecutive last-positive and first-zero body records establish displacement into death; velocity, held input and later lifecycle publication alone are not used as proof.",
    "No HP, position, action, physics, fatal/lifecycle, effect, palette, timer or outcome writes. Initial positive-HP fixture is explicitly disabled. No state LOAD, inventory grant or campaign prerequisite is used.",
    "Original blue X and gold Zero FX11 frame/shape pixels, palette and actual referenced GPU packets are compared against pinned original resources. Fatal body poses and all30 composed captures were root inspected. Packet observations and read-only bodies are nearby independent reads, not an instruction-atomic whole-machine claim.",
    "All visible owned death effects disappear naturally, with more than300 native updates observed and accepted survivor movement afterward. Original radial records can remain allocated but invisible (32 in this implementation); this is not a claim that every pool slot is freed, and no cleanup flags are forced.",
    "Reference matches cover the actual rendered native bursts, not every possible animation frame or a full framebuffer equality claim. Native contact can obscure the fatal body against an enemy; the retained composed capture and typed body are separate evidence.",
    "Ordinary finalized recording, exact declared sources/manifest, unchanged native cards, agreed profile, matching post-case CRCs and graceful exits0 are required. Historical failed/idle-hit attempts remain unchanged. No audio, other-stage/roster, remote-platform or separate content-audit credit."
